          "merged_at": "2026-06-14T18:35:21Z"
        },
        "body": "move_before_or_after resolved the destination from the moved node's parent instead of the target's parent. when the node and the target were in different groups this took the wrong branch (it moved the node to the tail of its own group) and also skipped the child count and parent updates, so the node was spliced across lists with a stale parent. a following move could then send the node back to its old group.\n\nnow it resolves the target's parent like scsynth does. added a test that compares the resulting tree on scsynth and supernova for cross group n_after and a double move.\n\ncloses #5909",
